# Denali tour execution and driver wallet settlement

## Scope of the first delivery

This delivery replaces no money flow. It introduces a durable, tenant-isolated
operational truth for the day of a tour:

```text
TourExecution → DriverExecutionFact → audited actual passenger count
```

It deliberately excludes wallet credit, withdrawal destination storage, reserve
management, and bank payout. Those commands require a later finance review and
their own migration/acceptance suite.

## Non-negotiable boundaries

- Tour publishing/sales lifecycle is not TourExecution. Execution has its own
  `scheduled | in_progress | completed | cancelled` state.
- A transport allocation is planning data only; it never proves actual carried
  passengers and never changes money.
- Every execution record is tenant-scoped, persisted under RLS and carries a
  version for optimistic concurrency.
- Updating actual count is operational only. It emits audit facts but no wallet,
  ledger, payout or notification side effect.
- `actualPassengerCount` begins at zero, is a non-negative integer, and cannot
  exceed the snapshotted offered passenger capacity.

## First-delivery HTTP contract

| Method | Path                                               | Purpose                                         |
| ------ | -------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- |
| GET    | `/tours/:tourId/execution`                         | Read execution and driver facts for the tenant. |
| POST   | `/tours/:tourId/execution/start`                   | Idempotently begin execution.                   |
| PATCH  | `/tours/:tourId/execution/drivers/:registrationId` | Versioned update of attendance/count.           |
| POST   | `/tours/:tourId/execution/complete`                | Mark execution completed; no financial effect.  |

All write commands require the existing operator session in this first slice.
The follow-up must introduce separate execution and finance permissions before
any wallet-credit command lands.

## Required proof

- PostgreSQL migration with RLS and tenant-scoped uniqueness.
- API tests: happy path, validation, replay, stale version, completion guard,
  cross-tenant denial and restart/persistence.
- No finance or WalletTransaction mutation in this slice.

## Explicitly deferred

- Calculating/confirming settlement from actual count.
- Wallet credit/reversal and member-wallet UI.
- Payment-destination encryption, withdrawal reservation, approval and payment.
- Telegram/SMS notifications for execution changes.

## Operator UI boundary

The operator workspace exposes an `execution` tab beside the operational roster.
It is usable on mobile and may start, update, and complete an execution only for
the existing admin/owner roles. The UI displays the driver identity from the
operational roster, but treats the execution API as the source of truth for
attendance and actual passenger counts. It must never display a credit action,
wallet balance, withdrawal destination, or a financial amount in this delivery.
